| artifacts/ | During this class, I completed numerous assignments focused on CompTIA A+ concepts, including computer hardware, software, operating systems, networking, security, and troubleshooting. I also created and maintained a GitHub portfolio to organize and showcase my work. Additional projects included developing a toolkit for IT support tasks, exploring workplace and computer safety practices, and learning how to use AI responsibly for problem-solving, research, and technical support. These artifacts demonstrate my growth in technical knowledge, organization, and professional skills.

| reflection/ | This course provided me with a strong foundation in information technology and prepared me for future studies related to the CompTIA A+ Core 1 and Core 2 certifications. Throughout the class, I completed many assignments that helped me understand computer hardware, software, operating systems, networking, security, and troubleshooting. Each assignment built my knowledge and gave me practical experience with concepts that are important in the IT field.

One of the most valuable parts of this course was working through CompTIA-related materials. These activities helped me become familiar with industry standards and the skills needed to support and maintain computer systems. I learned how to identify common hardware and software issues, apply troubleshooting techniques, and understand the importance of security and safety in technology environments.

Another important accomplishment was creating and maintaining a GitHub portfolio. This allowed me to organize my work, track my progress, and showcase the projects and assignments I completed throughout the course. Learning to use GitHub gave me experience with a tool that is widely used in technology careers and helped me develop better organizational skills.

I also gained experience designing and using AI tools responsibly. Through class activities, I learned how AI can assist with research, problem-solving, and productivity while understanding the importance of using these tools ethically and critically. In addition, I learned about workplace and computer safety practices, including how to protect equipment, data, and users from potential risks.

Overall, this course increased my confidence in my technical abilities and strengthened my interest in pursuing a career in information technology. The knowledge and skills I gained have prepared me to continue studying for the CompTIA A+ Core 1 and Core 2 certifications and to take on more advanced IT challenges in the future.

## What I Learned
In Computing Fundamentals, I developed a strong understanding of basic computer hardware, software, operating systems, and troubleshooting concepts. This course prepared me to continue my studies toward the CompTIA A+ Core 1 and Core 2 certifications by building the technical knowledge and problem-solving skills needed for IT support and computer maintenance.
